# [item 3 / GPU render] the runtime env that makes the stewie-gazebo image render on the NVIDIA GPU instead
# of software mesa. Discovered 2026-07-04: the image bakes ENV LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1 (correct for CPU-only
# CI), which FORCES software GL and segfaults OGRE2 when the nvidia GL libs are also mounted. Overriding it to
# 0 + putting the CDI-mounted nvidia GL on the loader path + forcing the nvidia GLX vendor + an xvfb display
# makes the gpu_lidar render + publish /model/ipex/perception/points (verified). Requires Aaron's docker
# features.cdi=true (2026-07-04) so `--device nvidia.com/gpu=all` mounts the nvidia GL userspace.
#
# Usage:
#   docker run --rm --device nvidia.com/gpu=all --env-file deploy/ros2/render_gpu.env \
#     stewie-gazebo:jazzy bash -lc 'echo /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/nvidia/current >/etc/ld.so.conf.d/nvidia.conf; \
#       ldconfig; xvfb-run -a gz sim -s -r --headless-rendering <world.sdf>'
NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES=all
LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=0
LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/nvidia/current
__GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=nvidia
